quran[10]{c,v,t}:
  16,55,"showing ingratitude for what We have given them. So enjoy for a while, for you will soon know."
  16,56,And they dedicate to those (idols) whom they do not know a share of what We have provided them. By Allah! You will indeed be questioned about (the lies) you used to fabricate.
  16,57,And they attribute daughters to Allah—Glory be to Him—while for themselves is what they desire (i.e. sons).
  16,58,"And whenever one of them is given the news of (the birth of) a baby girl, his face darkens as he suppresses his rage."
  16,59,"He hides from the people because of the evil of the news he has been given. Shall he keep it in disgrace or bury it (alive) in the dust? Indeed, evil is the judgement they make!"
  16,60,"For those who do not believe in the Hereafter, there is an evil example. And the finest exalted example belongs only to Allah. And He is the All-Mighty, the All-Wise."
  16,61,"If Allah were to punish people (immediately) for their wrongdoing, He would not leave a single moving creature on the earth, but He would reprieve them till an appointed time. So, when their time arrives, they cannot defer (it) by a moment, nor can they advance (it)."
  16,62,"And they attribute to Allah what they dislike (for themselves), and their tongues utter the lie that the best (things) belong to them. Undoubtedly, for them shall be the Fire, and they will be hastened into it (to be abandoned therein)."
  16,63,"By Allah! We have certainly sent (messengers) to (many) nations before you. But Satan made their deeds fair-seeming to them. So, he is their guardian today. And there is a painful punishment for them."
  16,64,"And We did not reveal the Book to you, except that you might clarify to them what they differ on, and as a guidance and a mercy for a people who believe."
